Below is a ready‑to‑paste template that shows how to call the **ChartSeriesGenerator** function with your own data.  
Just replace the placeholder strings with the real values from your project.

```javascript
// 1️⃣  Prepare your data (replace the placeholders with your actual arrays / objects)
const axisLabelsArray   = ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr'];          // <-- your axis labels
const dataPointsArray   = [120, 150, 170, 200];                 // <-- your data points
const defaultColor      = '#4287f5';                            // <-- your default color
const chartLayoutObject = {                                      // <-- your chart layout
  title: 'Monthly Sales',
  xAxis: { label: 'Month' },
  yAxis: { label: 'Revenue ($)' }
};

// 2️⃣  Convert the values to the string representations expected by the tool
const labelsString   = JSON.stringify(axisLabelsArray);   // e.g. "['Jan','Feb','Mar','Apr']"
const dataString     = JSON.stringify(dataPointsArray);   // e.g. "[120,150,170,200]"
const colorString    = defaultColor;                      // already a string
const layoutString   = JSON.stringify(chartLayoutObject); // e.g. '{"title":"Monthly Sales", ...}'

// 3️⃣  Call the function
const newSeries = ChartSeriesGenerator({
  labels: labelsString,
  data: dataString,
  color: colorString,
  chartLayout: layoutString
});

// 4️⃣  Use the returned series (e.g., add it to your chart)
chartLayoutObject.series = chartLayoutObject.series || [];
chartLayoutObject.series.push(newSeries);
```

### What each part does

| Step | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| **1️⃣** | Define your actual data. Replace the example arrays/objects with your real values. |
| **2️⃣** | Convert the JavaScript objects/arrays into *string* representations because the `ChartSeriesGenerator` expects strings. |
| **3️⃣** | Invoke the function with those stringified values. |
| **4️⃣** | Attach the newly created series to your chart layout. |

Feel free to copy this snippet into your codebase and adjust the placeholder values. If you run into any issues or need further customization (e.g., multiple series, custom colors per point), let me know!
